        "original_id": "4a9a9d7a-40fb-54ff-85f5-88e0ac255656",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Christopher Mont, Thomas Cromwell, Henry VIII\n- Places: Koblenz, England\n- Roles: diplomat, agent, lawyer, statesman, chief minister, king\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Mont was born in 1496 or 1497 in Koblenz.\n- Thomas Cromwell was born in 1485.\n- In 1531, Christopher Mont was awarded denization in England.\n- In 1531, Christopher Mont became an agent of Thomas Cromwell in England.\n- From 1532 to 1540, Thomas Cromwell served as chief minister to King Henry VIII of England.\n- Thomas Cromwell was an English lawyer and statesman.\n- Christopher Mont was a sixteenth-century diplomat.\n- Thomas Cromwell was the 1st Earl of Essex.\n- Thomas Cromwell died on 28 July 1540.\n- Christopher Mont died in 1572.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
